  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response to extraordinary risks generated by violence and improving reception conditions for refugees and migrants entering and transiting through Honduras.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide critical protection support to vulnerable communities affected by displacement. This UNHCR project delivers cash assistance, psychological and health support, and protection support for children, as well as creates safe spaces for displaced individuals and prevents risks against life, security, freedom, and personal integrity of IDPs, asylum-seekers, refugees, and other persons with protection needs. The project provides life-saving protection to 10,855 individuals, including 3,199 women, 4,544 men, 3,112 children, and 543 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
